      "name": "knowledge-header-list-association",
      "statement": "Knowledge header list association is repaired: only empty-value keys own following block items; scalar and inline values close association, and malformed scalar answers remain visible to denial. Identical20-case/80-assertion public checker proof changes16 original REDs/64 controls to all GREEN. Three actual source controls fail14/2/16 with complete plans and exact restoration; two semantic evidence corruptions reject and restore. Full original1485 Markdown inputs/1349 facts are retained in a recoverable capsule; the current full gate passes with six planned header overlays and unchanged fact bodies. Original534 bindings/full123810-byte callback publication and actual readonly baseline are preserved at328b11c5. Book89 inputs/four render controls pass.",
      "scope": "This is the existing Knowledge doctrine list-association boundary, its public generator/checker fixture and canonical selection. The full original scan bytes are capsule inputs; six current card overlays, exact current source identities and map are independently checked by the reader. Historical callback bindings are recovered from accepted Git without refreshing their native observations. Current reverify routes retain all prior header routes and original body prefixes. The first source-control producer fails because its third mutation reverses rather than disables the verdict, yielding14/2/34 failures; its source/full observations/actual outer1 remain immutable. A distinct producer changes that operator and output identity only, yielding14/2/16 and restored GREEN. Complete actual tool logs and native separate channels are retained. Two public valid block metadata cases reproduce missing evidence/reverify projection; P3 PERL-PRIVATE-FACTORY-CAPTURE.3.2.1.12 owns the field contract and affected population after factory/pipeline, before TYPE-REFERENCE-BOOK. No complete YAML/field-type, new runtime, private parent or other-backend admission is claimed. The exact staged canonical receipt is the required landing boundary, separate from this focused retained measurement. No immutable toolchain or cross-version HTML identity is claimed.",
